It simply stopped passing traffic. A simple "ifdown eth1 ; ifup eth1" brought it back up.
eth0 was working perfectly.

x86_64 kernel, Athlon 64X2 3800, Asus M2N32-WS PRO board, 4GB Ram
Machine was lightly loaded as far as I could tell.

dmesg snip, ifconfig, /proc/net/dev, lspci -vv, /proc/interrupts attached.

Machine has been up 4 days and is brand spanking new, so I have no idea if this is an old issue.
There is about another 4 or 5 times this amount of dmesg there, but totaling 441k I thought it a bit 
excessive to post.

Not subscribed to netdev, if there is anything else I can provide please let me know.

Regards,
Brad

